    "diff_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pull/3.diff",
    "patch_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pull/3.patch",
    "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/issues/3",
    "number": 3,
    "state": "closed",
    "locked": false,
    "title": "Fix AdaptiveSemaphore instability and Orchestrator safety issues",
    "user": {
      "login": "1h0lde4",
      "id": 196927701,
      "node_id": "U_kgDOC7zg1Q",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/196927701?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/following{/other_user}",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/gists{/gist_id}",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/starred{/owner}{/repo}",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/events{/privacy}",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "user_view_type": "public",
      "site_admin": false
    },
    "body": "I have identified and fixed several critical bugs related to system stability and resilience:\n\n1. **AdaptiveSemaphore Instability**: The concurrency controller was oscillating wildly (thrashing) due to a race condition (using instance-level instead of task-level start times) and a lack of hysteresis. I refactored it to use `contextvars`, added a 10% deadband, and smoothed the adjustment logic. I also implemented a proper permit-shrinking mechanism that was previously missing.\n2. **Orchestrator Robustness**: Added null checks for `self.context` in the main `handle` loop to prevent `AttributeError` crashes during edge cases like task cancellation or incomplete initialization.\n3. **Verification**: \n   - `tests/break_adaptive_thrash.py` now shows stable steady-state behavior.\n   - `tests/break_cancellation.py` no longer triggers `AttributeError`.\n   - All 114 standard tests in the suite are passing.\n\n---\n*PR created automatically by Jules for task [12275271135949836668](https://jules.google.com/task/12275271135949836668) started by @1h0lde4*",
    "created_at": "2026-06-03T20:47:05Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-06-18T13:08:56Z",
